#: ../../whatsnew/3.11.rst:389
msgid "PEP 681: Data class transforms"
msgstr "PEP 681: Datenklassen-Transformationen"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.11.rst:391
msgid ""
":deco:`~typing.dataclass_transform` may be used to decorate a class, "
"metaclass, or a function that is itself a decorator. The presence of "
"``@dataclass_transform()`` tells a static type checker that the decorated "
"object performs runtime \"magic\" that transforms a class, giving "
"it :func:`dataclass <dataclasses.dataclass>`-like behaviors."
msgstr ""
":deco:`~typing.dataclass_transform` kann verwendet werden, um eine Klasse, "
"eine Metaklasse oder eine Funktion zu dekorieren, die selbst ein Dekorator "
"ist. Das Vorhandensein von ``@dataclass_transform()`` teilt einem statischen "
"Typprüfer mit, dass das dekorierte Objekt zur Laufzeit „Magie“ ausführt, die "
"eine Klasse umwandelt und ihr ein :func:`dataclass <dataclasses.dataclass>`-"
"ähnliches Verhalten gibt."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.11.rst:397
msgid "For example::"
msgstr "Zum Beispiel::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.11.rst:399
msgid ""
"# The create_model decorator is defined by a library.\n"
"@typing.dataclass_transform()\n"
"def create_model(cls: Type[T]) -> Type[T]:\n"
"    cls.__init__ = ...\n"
"    cls.__eq__ = ...\n"
"    cls.__ne__ = ...\n"
"    return cls\n"
"\n"
"# The create_model decorator can now be used to create new model classes:\n"
"@create_model\n"
"class CustomerModel:\n"
"    id: int\n"
"    name: str\n"
"\n"
"c = CustomerModel(id=327, name=\"Eric Idle\")"
msgstr ""
"# The create_model decorator is defined by a library.\n"
"@typing.dataclass_transform()\n"
"def create_model(cls: Type[T]) -> Type[T]:\n"
"    cls.__init__ = ...\n"
"    cls.__eq__ = ...\n"
"    cls.__ne__ = ...\n"
"    return cls\n"
"\n"
"# The create_model decorator can now be used to create new model classes:\n"
"@create_model\n"
"class CustomerModel:\n"
"    id: int\n"
"    name: str\n"
"\n"
"c = CustomerModel(id=327, name=\"Eric Idle\")"

